      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "**Multi-Agency Coordination and Communication**\n\nDuring the initial phase, establishing clear communication is an **immediate** priority to prevent radio clutter and ensure operational synchronization. Fire Command must designate a single Incident Commander, whose directives are **critical** for all agencies. Police units must establish a secure perimeter, issuing a **warning** to the public regarding the **danger** zone, while EMS teams maintain a clear staging area for **urgent** patient triage. All inter-agency updates must be concise, utilizing pre-established communication protocols to maintain a high level of operational readiness.",
      "source": "target",
